💡 BEST PRACTICES AND NOTES
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

1. INCLUSIVE RANGE:
   • BETWEEN includes both endpoints
   • Equivalent: column BETWEEN a AND b is same as column >= a AND column <= b

2. DATA TYPE MATCHING:
   • Use the correct type for the boundary values
   • Numeric range: BETWEEN 10 AND 20
   • Date range: BETWEEN '1996-07-01' AND '1996-07-31'
   • Text range: BETWEEN 'A' AND 'Z'

3. TEXT ORDERING:
   • Text BETWEEN uses collation rules for alphabetical sorting
   • Make sure the strings are in correct lexicographic order

4. NULL VALUES:
   • BETWEEN excludes NULL values
   • Use IS NULL if you want to include null records separately

5. NOT BETWEEN AND NULL:
   • A NULL boundary or NULL column value may produce no rows
   • Example: WHERE Price NOT BETWEEN 10 AND NULL returns unknown

6. PERFORMANCE:
   • BETWEEN is usually efficient on indexed numeric and date columns
   • It is equivalent to two range comparisons

7. COMBINING WITH OTHER CONDITIONS:
   • BETWEEN works well with IN, LIKE, AND, OR, and joins
   • Example: WHERE Price BETWEEN 10 AND 20 AND CategoryID IN (1,2,3)

8. DATE RANGE INCLUSIVITY:
   • For date/time fields with time parts, include the end-of-day if needed
   • Example: WHERE created_at BETWEEN '2024-05-01' AND '2024-05-31 23:59:59'


═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
⚠️ COMMON BETWEEN OPERATOR MISTAKES
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

1. Reversed boundaries:
   ❌ WRONG: WHERE Price BETWEEN 20 AND 10
   ❌ RESULT: No rows returned
   ✓ CORRECT: WHERE Price BETWEEN 10 AND 20

2. Using VARCHAR dates with wrong format:
   ❌ WRONG: WHERE OrderDate BETWEEN '07-01-1996' AND '07-31-1996'
   ✓ CORRECT: WHERE OrderDate BETWEEN '1996-07-01' AND '1996-07-31'

3. Assuming NOT BETWEEN returns only values outside range but includes NULL:
   ❌ WRONG: WHERE Price NOT BETWEEN 10 AND 20
   • NULL values are not returned unless explicitly included with OR Price IS NULL

4. Using BETWEEN for non-sequential text values:
   ❌ WRONG: WHERE ProductName BETWEEN 'Z' AND 'A'
   ✓ CORRECT: WHERE ProductName BETWEEN 'A' AND 'Z'

5. Ignoring time when filtering datetime columns:
   ❌ WRONG: WHERE created_at BETWEEN '2024-05-01' AND '2024-05-31'
   • This may exclude rows on 2024-05-31 with time > 00:00:00


